":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S001\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix an arbitrary compact K⊂ℝⁿ to establish finiteness of Lebesgue measure on every compact set.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"n\"]},{\"symbol\":\"R₀\",\"type\":\"positive real\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S001\",\"kind\":\"witness\",\"declaration\":\"Choose R₀>0 such that K is contained in the closed Euclidean ball of radius R₀, using M016 and the definition of boundedness.\",\"from_inputs\":[\"M016\"],\"from_local\":[\"K\"],\"objects\":[\"K\"]},{\"symbol\":\"Q\",\"type\":\"closed coordinate box [-R₀,R₀]^n\",\"scope\":\"R002\",\"start\":\"S001\",\"end\":\"S001\",\"kind\":\"definition\",\"declaration\":\"Set Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀].\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[\"R₀\"],\"objects\":[\"R₀\",\"n\"]}]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/argument/0/text\",\"value\":\"Fix arbitrary t>0, put J=[t/2,3t/2], and choose compact C from H003 so u(x,s)=q for every x∉C and s∈J. First establish the ambient measure fact needed for M001. Fix arbitrary compact K⊂ℝⁿ. By M016 it is bounded, so choose R₀>0 with K contained in the closed Euclidean ball of radius R₀. Every coordinate of a point in that ball has absolute value at most R₀, so K⊆Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀]. The set K is closed, hence Borel measurable in the Euclidean Borel measurable space. M013 computes the Lebesgue measure of Q as the product of the coordinate interval measures; M014 gives each factor as 2R₀. Thus μ(Q)=(2R₀)^n<∞, and monotonicity gives μ(K)≤μ(Q)<∞. Since K was arbitrary, Lebesgue measure on ℝⁿ is finite on compact sets. This also establishes the needed measurable-topological ambient: the measurable space is the Borel σ-algebra generated by Euclidean open sets, so every open set is measurable. Joint smoothness and the fact u=q on the open spatial complement of C throughout J imply, for all s∈J, every first spatial and time derivative vanishes outside C; differentiating these constant-zero fields in the open complement shows the second and mixed derivatives used in e_t also vanish there. Therefore e(·,t) is continuous with compact support in C. The real scalars form a normed additive commutative group, and the preceding ambient argument supplies all measure hypotheses of M001; apply M001 to obtain integrability of e(·,t). The same support reasoning gives continuity and vanishing off C for u_t, u_{x_j}, e and e_t throughout J. This proves all the claims in N001 for arbitrary t.\"}]} }","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"5867090b-ddde-4120-a7d3-b73fd49d4f83","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":130934,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":129664,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1254,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":339},"total_tokens":132188,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb41c23d4c8191ad23decc9cc2155e":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":31,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb41c580d8819183aa0cdc0086b155":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":34,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb41c772788191afa6cbc484ea7182":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":34,"cache_write_tokens